1
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Her world. Her secrets. Her legacy.

2
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Black Widow is a action, adventure, science fiction
film directed by Cate Shortland.

3
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Natasha Romanoff, also known as Black Widow, confronts the darker parts of her
ledger when a dangerous conspiracy with ties to her past arises.

4
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Pursued by a force that will stop at nothing to bring her down, Natasha must deal with her history as a
spy and the broken relationships left in her wake long before she became an Avenger.

5
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Natasha Romanoff / Black Widow, played by Scarlett Johansson.

6
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Yelena Belova, played by Florence Pugh.

7
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Melina, played by Rachel Weisz.

8
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Alexei, played by David Harbour.

9
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Dreykov, played by Ray Winstone.

10
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:46,000
Young Natasha, played by Ever Anderson.

11
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Black Widow is a 2021 American superhero film based on Marvel
Comics featuring the character of the same name.

12
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion
Pictures, it is the 24th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:10,000
The film was directed by Cate Shortland from a screenplay by Eric Pearson and stars Scarlett Johansson as Natasha Romanoff / Black
Widow alongside Florence Pugh, David Harbour, O-T Fagbenle, Olga Kurylenko, William Hurt, Ray Winstone, and Rachel Weisz.

14
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:38,000
Mostly set during the events of Captain America: Civil War (2016), the film sees Romanoff on the
run and forced to confront her past as a Russian spy before she became an Avenger.

15
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
Lionsgate Films began developing a Black Widow film in April 2004,
with David Hayter attached to write and direct.

16
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
The project did not move forward and the character's film
rights had reverted to Marvel Studios by June 2006.

17
01:15:56,000 --> 01:16:02,000
Johansson was cast in the role for several MCU films beginning with Iron
Man 2 (2010), and began discussing a solo film with Marvel.

18
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:30,000
Work began in late 2017 and Shortland was hired in July 2018.

19
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:58,000
Jac Schaeffer and Ned Benson contributed to the script before Pearson joined.

20
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
The film was written to be a prequel that expands on Romanoff's history and helps end her
MCU story following the character's death in Avengers: Endgame (2019).

21
01:33:48,000 --> 01:33:54,000
Shortland put an emphasis on the fight sequences and said
this was the most violent MCU film so far.

22
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:22,000
Filming took place from May to October 2019 in Norway,
England, Budapest, Morocco, and Macon, Georgia.

23
01:42:44,000 --> 01:42:50,000
Black Widow premiered at events around the world on June 29, 2021, and was released in the United
States on July 9, simultaneously in theaters and through Disney+ with Premier Access.

24
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
It is the first film in Phase Four of the MCU, and was delayed three times from
an original May 2020 release date due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

25
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:46,000
Black Widow broke several pandemic box office records
and grossed over $379 million worldwide.

26
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:14,000
The film received positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for the
action sequences and for the performances of Johansson and Pugh.

27
02:00:36,000 --> 02:00:42,000
In July 2021, Johansson filed a lawsuit against Disney over the
simultaneous release, which was settled two months later.

28
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:10,000
The film explores themes of assassin, hero, spy, kgb, based on comic.

29
02:09:32,000 --> 02:09:38,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
